@namespace Fdw.UI.Components

@* Why: the utility classes the Fdw UI packages emit are defined in a static web asset that ships
   with Fdw.UI.Components, and a NuGet package cannot add a <link> to the host's App.razor. Rendering
   the link from a component the host already renders is what lets the class definitions arrive with
   the package instead of having to be re-declared in every skin.

   Why the link sits in the body rather than in <HeadContent>: HeadOutlet lives in App.razor at the
   host's chosen render mode, which need not be the render mode of the tree that declares the head
   content, and a stylesheet that silently fails to load is a whole-console visual regression. A
   <link rel="stylesheet"> element in the body applies to the document under every render mode, and
   carries display:none from the UA stylesheet so it never participates in layout.

   Order does not matter: every rule in the asset is !important and no host rule in this cascade
   layer is, so the utilities keep the precedence the inline style attributes they replaced had. *@

